1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:08,485
Metis Check for ChatGPT and Codex. Checks the citations in an answer at the registries that issue them. Every check files a signed report anyone can recheck.

2
00:00:09,267 --> 00:00:15,929
Free: 5 checks a month. Pro and Team on the same page. No prices inside the plugin.

3
00:00:21,267 --> 00:00:26,407
Connect: sign in once with a Metis account. One account covers ChatGPT, Codex and Claude.

4
00:00:33,267 --> 00:00:41,477
Ask: is this DOI real? Metis asks Crossref, the agency that registered it. Settled true, with a report.

5
00:00:49,267 --> 00:01:00,487
Ask: check this LEI for Apple Inc. Metis asks GLEIF and compares the name. Settled true.

6
00:01:05,267 --> 00:01:17,205
Ask: check the citations in this paragraph. Every identifier is found at its position and checked. Three on record. One DOI is not: settled false.

7
00:01:25,267 --> 00:01:33,207
Ask: check this ROR id for MIT. Metis asks the Research Organization Registry. Settled true, under the name given.

8
00:01:41,267 --> 00:01:48,001
Ask: open my report and tell me whether its signature still verifies. Every item, the rechecks since, and signature verified: true.

9
00:01:57,267 --> 00:02:02,630
Ask it to check a whole conversation: no tool is called. Metis checks a passage you give it.

10
00:02:06,267 --> 00:02:11,781
Give it a bare number: it asks what the number is. Metis never guesses an identifier's type.

11
00:02:15,267 --> 00:02:21,763
Ask whether a paper proves your point: Metis reports the registration and what Crossref holds. It does not grade the argument.

12
00:02:25,267 --> 00:02:36,479
Every report: unique id, registry query per line, a recheck button anyone can press, PDF and signed JSON.

13
00:02:56,267 --> 00:03:02,251
The verification engine behind Metis Check comes from Metis's proprietary methods, developed through government-grade research.

14
00:03:03,267 --> 00:03:10,922
Metis Check by Metis Foundry. Add it in ChatGPT, Codex, Claude or Claude Code. hello@metisfoundry.com

